---
title: Passkeys — WebAuthn Enrolment & Sign-In
---
%% Public-key authentication. The private key never leaves the authenticator, so there is no
%% shared secret for this app to store, leak, or have phished.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant AUTH as Authenticator<br/>Touch ID / Windows Hello / key
    participant SPA as Angular<br/>webauthn.utils
    participant API as PasskeyController<br/>/user/webauthn
    participant STORE as WebAuthnChallengeStore
    participant DB as MySQL
    participant SESS as SessionService

    rect rgba(107, 91, 255, 0.10)
    note over U, SESS: Enrolment — signed in already
    U->>SPA: "Add a passkey"
    SPA->>API: POST /user/webauthn/enroll/options
    API->>STORE: mintForRegistration(challenge)
    STORE->>DB: INSERT webauthnchallenges
    note right of STORE: Was an in-memory map until 2026-08-29 —<br/>a challenge minted on one instance could<br/>never be redeemed on another.
    API-->>SPA: PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions
    SPA->>AUTH: navigator.credentials.create()
    AUTH->>U: Biometric / PIN prompt
    U->>AUTH: Approve
    AUTH-->>SPA: Attestation + PUBLIC key
    SPA->>API: POST /user/webauthn/enroll/complete
    API->>STORE: redeem(challenge) — single use
    API->>DB: Store credential id, public key, sign counter
    API-->>SPA: 200 — passkey registered
    end

    rect rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.10)
    note over U, SESS: Sign-in — no password involved
    U->>SPA: "Sign in with a passkey"
    SPA->>API: POST /user/verify/webauthn/options
    API->>STORE: mintForAuthentication(challenge)
    API-->>SPA: allowCredentials + challenge
    SPA->>AUTH: navigator.credentials.get()
    AUTH->>U: Biometric / PIN prompt
    U->>AUTH: Approve
    AUTH-->>SPA: Assertion signed by the PRIVATE key
    note right of AUTH: The private key never leaves the device.<br/>Nothing phishable crosses the network.
    SPA->>API: POST /user/verify/webauthn
    API->>STORE: redeem(challenge)
    API->>DB: Verify signature against the stored public key
    API->>DB: Check + advance the sign counter
    note right of API: A counter that went backwards suggests<br/>a cloned authenticator.

    alt verification fails
        API-->>SPA: 401
    else verified
        API->>SESS: issueTokenPair(...)
        API-->>SPA: 200 {access_token, refresh_token}
        SPA->>U: Navigate to dashboard
    end
    end

    note over U, SESS: Passkeys deliberately bypass risk-based step-up: possession of the<br/>authenticator is already stronger evidence than an emailed code.
